+## 16. Function reference
+
+Signatures as they stand today. The code is the fact; fix this list when it drifts.
+
+- `parseAmount(input: string): Cents` in `src/money.ts` trims the input, drops a leading `$`,
+  accepts an optional minus sign, digits and at most two fractional digits, and returns integer
+  cents. Anything else throws `Invalid amount: <input>`.
+- `formatAmount(cents: Cents): string` in `src/money.ts` prints two fractional digits and a leading
+  `-` for a negative value, with no thousands separator.
+- `Ledger` in `src/ledger.ts`: `add(entry)` validates and appends, `entries` is a read-only view,
+  `balance(account?)` sums everything or one account, and `monthlyTotals()` returns a
+  `Map<string, Cents>` keyed `YYYY-MM` in chronological order.
+- `parseCsv(text: string): Entry[]` in `src/csv.ts` checks the header, splits each row following
+  RFC 4180, requires four columns, trims the cells and converts the amount with `parseAmount`.
+- `Importer`, `IMPORTERS` and `importerFor(id)` in `src/importers/index.ts` form the registry. An
+  unknown id throws and lists the known ones. `ledgerCsvImporter` wraps `parseCsv`; the Bank B
+  importer lives in `src/importers/bank-b.ts`.
+- `renderTable(columns, rows, options?)` in `src/report.ts` pads every column to its widest cell (or
+  its `minWidth`), joins the columns with the gutter (two spaces by default) and underlines the
+  header with dashes.
+- `summarizeAccounts(entries)` returns, per account, the entry count, income, expenses and balance,
+  sorted by account name.
+- `summarizeMonths(entries)` returns, per month, the entry count, the total and the largest
+  expense of the month when it has one, in chronological order.
+- `share(part, whole)` is the percentage of `part` in `whole` with one decimal, and 0 when `whole`
+  is 0. It is the only place a ratio is computed.
+- `categorize(entry, rules?)` returns the category of the first matching rule, or `Other`.
+- `summarizeCategories(entries, rules?)` returns the expense total of each category and its share
+  of all expenses; income entries are excluded.
+- `renderAccountReport`, `renderMonthReport` and `renderCategoryReport` produce the text the CLI
+  prints for `accounts`, `months` and `categories`.
+- `runningBalance(entries)` returns the balance after each entry, in the order given.
+- `recurringEntries(entries, minMonths = 2)` is described in section 3.4.
+- `run(argv)` and `USAGE` in `src/cli.ts` are described in section 8.
